# Loop engine routing — copy to .env (gitignored, machine-specific) and edit.
# Everything here is OPTIONAL: with no .env, every role runs on frontier:high
# (= your real Claude). You only add variables to deviate.

# Which tool drives the fleet:  claude | codex | opencode   (codex/opencode = stubs for now)
LOOP_TOOL=claude

# ── Engine = provider:tier ────────────────────────────────────────────
# providers:  frontier (real Anthropic / subscription) | glm (OpenRouter via ccr) | local (Ollama via ccr)
# tiers:      high | mid | low   (opus | sonnet | haiku accepted as aliases)
#   frontier: high→opus  mid→sonnet  low→haiku
#   glm:      high/mid→glm-5.2  low→glm-4.7
#   local:    →qwen3.6:27b (one model)
# Phase 2 will add failover chains, e.g.  LOOP_ENGINE_DEFAULT="frontier:high|glm:high"
# (QUOTE any value containing '|' — .env is shell-sourced and a bare | is a pipe.)
# Note: glm/local require `ccr` on PATH and the box/key reachable, else they're skipped.

# Default for any role left unset (omit → frontier:high):
#LOOP_ENGINE_DEFAULT=frontier:high

# Per-role overrides — roles: planner, researcher, engineer, verifier, integrator
#LOOP_ENGINE_ENGINEER=local:high
#LOOP_ENGINE_VERIFIER=frontier:high   # NOTE: verifier stays frontier even if you never set it
# Engine routing controls the TOP-LEVEL role calls — the executor (run-plan.sh, role
# 'engineer') and the auditor (verify.sh, role 'verifier'); their agent files use
# `model: inherit` so the routed --model wins. Sub-agents spawned *within* a run use
# their own frontmatter model (e.g. researcher = fixed haiku, cheap recon).

# ── Scenario recipes ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1) Frontier for everything (the default): set nothing.
# 3) Frontier plans + verifies, local writes code:
#      LOOP_ENGINE_ENGINEER=local:high
#      LOOP_ENGINE_RESEARCHER=local:high
#      (planner + verifier inherit/stay frontier)

# ── Endpoints / models (defaults shown; override only if your setup differs) ──
#CCR_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3456
#OLLAMA_HOST=ollama-gpu.home.arpa:11434
#LOCAL_MODEL=qwen3.6:27b
